        <mxCell id="eC9dH8ZyD7G253RybXqz-38" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;Arestas Dirigidas: E = {(A → B), (B → C), (C → A), (C → D), (D → B)}&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="30" width="340" x="250" y="545" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eC9dH8ZyD7G253RybXqz-39" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;Vértice: C&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;Grau de entrada: 1&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;C (a via B →&amp;nbsp; C)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;Grau de saída: 2&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;C (as vias C →&amp;nbsp; A e C →&amp;nbsp; D)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="160" width="230" x="305" y="610" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eC9dH8ZyD7G253RybXqz-40" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;Em um grafo não dirigido, as arestas são pares não ordenados {u, v}, o que significa que o percurso sempre pode ser feito em ambas as direções. Aplicar isso ao trânsito assume, falsamente, que todas as ruas de uma cidade são de mão dupla.&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
